    <bpmn:process id="W_W728" name="W728. Port &amp; Customs Clearance Daily Status Tracking &amp; Escalation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Start of supply chain operations day; or customs/broker status update
Frequency: Daily review; real-time status updates from customs broker
Volume: ~400–600 TEUs/month import containers; ~15–25 containers in clearance pipeline at any time
Owner: Import Coordinator
Participants: Customs Broker, Logistics Manager, Finance (LC/duty payments), Warehouse Manager
Source: workflow W728 — Port &amp; Customs Clearance Daily Status Tracking &amp; Escalation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W728_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W728_Lane1" name="Import Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W728_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W728_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W728_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W728_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W728_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W728_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W728_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W728_Start3" name="Start of supply chain operations day; or customs/broker status update">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W728_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W728_Task4" name="Morning import pipeline status review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Morning import pipeline status review: Import Coordinator reviews import pipeline dashboard: (a) vessels expected to arrive in next 7 days: vessel name, ETA, number of BuildRight containers, port of discharge (Manila South Harbor, Manila North Harbor, Cebu, Davao, Clark); (b) containers currently at port: days since vessel arrival, current clearance status (discharged, under customs examination, assessed, payment pending, released for haulage, gated out); (c) containers in transit to DC: estimated arrival at DC per W250 tracking; (d) containers exceeding standard clearance timeline (&gt;7 days from discharge): flag as potential demurrage risk per W249
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 20-30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W728_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W728_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W728_Task5" name="Customs broker status update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customs broker status update: Import Coordinator obtains daily status from customs broker: (a) for each container in clearance pipeline: (i) current status and next step; (ii) expected timeline for next milestone; (iii) any issues: missing documentation, customs hold, examination required, assessment dispute, BOC system downtime; (b) for containers requiring customs examination: (i) examination type: green lane (no exam), yellow lane (document exam), red lane (physical exam); (ii) red lane: coordinate with broker for examination scheduling, prepare supporting documentation; (iii) estimate additional clearance time for examinations; (c) document all status updates in tracking system with timestamps
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator / Customs Broker
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 15-30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W728_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W728_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W728_Task6" name="Escalation management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Escalation management: for containers stuck at specific stages: (a) stuck at discharge (&gt;2 days): contact shipping line for container availability; (b) stuck awaiting customs examination (&gt;3 days): escalate to broker for examination scheduling; contact BOC if broker unable to resolve; (c) stuck at assessment (&gt;2 days): verify all documentation submitted; escalate duty assessment disputes per W239; (d) stuck at payment: coordinate with Finance for immediate duty payment via IPAY/Pass5 per W239 step 1; (e) stuck at release (&gt;1 day after payment): escalate to broker for gate-out coordination; (f) for each escalation: document actions taken and timeline for resolution
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 15-30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W728_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W728_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W728_Task7" name="Supply chain impact assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Supply chain impact assessment: Import Coordinator communicates clearance timeline impact: (a) for containers carrying critical stock (A-items, promotional items per W57): notify Supply Chain Planner of expected DC receipt date; (b) assess impact on store replenishment: will clearance delays cause stockouts at stores?; (c) for promotional items: alert Merchandising if promotional launch per W13 may be affected by delayed import receipt; (d) for seasonal items per W32: assess whether seasonal buy will arrive in time for seasonal window
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator / Supply Chain Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 10-15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W728_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W728_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W728_Task8" name="Demurrage and storage cost monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Demurrage and storage cost monitoring: daily, Import Coordinator tracks cost exposure: (a) containers exceeding free time at port (typically 5-7 days free, then PHP 5,000-8,000/day demurrage): calculate daily cost exposure; (b) total monthly demurrage cost vs. budget; (c) identify root causes of demurrage incidents: documentation delays, customs holds, payment delays, carrier no-show for haulage; (d) demurrage cost data feeds into W680 supply chain cost analysis
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 10 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W728_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W728_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W728_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W728_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W728_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-244 (ensure controlled execution — Import &amp; Customs Operations (PA-02.2).) | - operational: Import Coordinator review and approval gate
Owner: Import Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W728_Assoc11" sourceRef="W728_Annotation10" targetRef="W728_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W728_Flow12" sourceRef="W728_Start3" targetRef="W728_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W728_Flow13" sourceRef="W728_Task4" targetRef="W728_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W728_Flow14" sourceRef="W728_Task5" targetRef="W728_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W728_Flow15" sourceRef="W728_Task6" targetRef="W728_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W728_Flow16" sourceRef="W728_Task7" targetRef="W728_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W728_Flow17" sourceRef="W728_Task8" targetRef="W728_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W728_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W728_plane" bpmnElement="W_W728">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W728_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_Task4_di" bpmnElement="W728_Task4"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W728_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W728_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W728_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W728_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_Start3_di" bpmnElement="W728_Start3"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_End9_di" bpmnElement="W728_End9"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W728_Annotation10_di" bpmnElement="W728_Annotation10"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="290" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W728_Flow12_di" bpmnElement="W728_Flow12"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W728_Flow13_di" bpmnElement="W728_Flow13"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W728_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W728_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="790" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W728_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W728_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W728_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W728_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W728_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W728_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W728_Assoc11_di" bpmnElement="W728_Assoc11"><di:waypoint x="340" y="290" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1233" name="W1233. Philippine Bureau of Customs Import Entry Processing &amp; Duty Assessment Automation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Import container arrival at Philippine port (Manila, Cebu, Davao, or Subic/Clark)
Frequency: ~400–600 TEUs/month; ~15–30 containers/working day
Volume: ~1,800–3,600 import entries/year across all import vendors (multiple TEUs consolidated per entry per W464)
Owner: Customs Broker / Import Specialist
Participants: Customs Broker, Import Specialist, Category Manager, Finance – Tax, Freight Forwarder, Bureau of Customs
Source: workflow W1233 — Philippine Bureau of Customs Import Entry Processing &amp; Duty Assessment Automation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1233_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1233_Lane1" name="Import Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1233_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1233_Lane3" name="Customs Broker">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1233_Lane4" name="Finance – Tax">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1233_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1233_Start6" name="Import container arrival at Philippine port (Manila, Cebu, Davao, or Subic/Clark)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1233_Task7" name="Shipment pre-arrival preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Shipment pre-arrival preparation: Import Specialist receives advance shipping documents from vendor/freight forwarder: (a) commercial invoice, (b) packing list, (c) bill of lading (B/L) or airway bill, (d) certificate of origin (if FTA claim), (e) import permit or clearance (for regulated items per W467)
Responsible (R): Import Specialist
Accountable (A): Customs Broker
Duration: 1–2 hours/entry</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1233_Task8" name="Automated HS code classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated HS code classification: ERP system auto-matches item SKUs to HS codes from item master (maintained per W293 tax master): (a) system validates HS code against BOC latest tariff schedule; (b) system checks for preferential tariff eligibility (ASEAN, ACFTA); (c) system flags items with classification ambiguity for Customs Broker review; (d) system calculates estimated duty: duty amount = CIF value × duty rate (0–30% depending on HS chapter)
Responsible (R): System / Import Specialist
Accountable (A): Customs Broker
Duration: 15 min/entry</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1233_Task9" name="Customs value declaration preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customs value declaration preparation: (a) system calculates CIF value: invoice value + freight + insurance; (b) add dutiable ancillary costs (royalties, assists, packaging); (c) deduct non-dutiable items where applicable; (d) generate customs value declaration worksheet with supporting documentation
Responsible (R): Import Specialist
Accountable (A): Customs Broker
Duration: 30 min/entry</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1233_Task10" name="BOC e2m (Electronic-to-Mobile) system filing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: BOC e2m (Electronic-to-Mobile) system filing: Customs Broker files import entry via BOC e2m system: (a) select entry type (formal consumption, informal, warehousing per W284); (b) upload HS classifications, quantities, and values; (c) attach supporting documents electronically; (d) system auto-calculates duties, VAT, and other charges; (e) select payment mode (direct debit via AAB, or cash/manager&#x27;s check)
Responsible (R): Customs Broker
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30–60 min/entry</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1233_Task11" name="Duty payment &amp; assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Duty payment &amp; assessment: (a) BOC assesses entry; system calculates total duty liability; (b) Customs Broker authorizes payment via accredited bank (BDO/BPI); (c) BOC issues Single Administrative Document (SAD) with assessment; (d) for select shipments: BOC Green Lane (auto-release), Yellow Lane (document check), or Red Lane (physical inspection)
Responsible (R): Customs Broker
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1233_Task12" name="Cargo release &amp; delivery order">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Cargo release &amp; delivery order: (a) once assessed and duty paid: BOC releases cargo; (b) Customs Broker obtains delivery order from shipping line; (c) arranges trucking from port to DC per W464; (d) system updates import PO status to &quot;Customs Cleared&quot; with duty and landed cost details
Responsible (R): Customs Broker / Import Specialist
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1233_Task13" name="Landed cost posting &amp; WAC update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Landed cost posting &amp; WAC update: (a) system calculates final landed cost per SKU: invoice cost + freight + insurance + duty + port charges + brokerage fees; (b) system posts landed cost to inventory receipt per W3; (c) WAC recalculated for received quantity; (d) duty and VAT posted to appropriate GL accounts per W90
Responsible (R): System / Finance – Tax
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1233_Task14" name="Monthly duty reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly duty reconciliation: Finance – Tax reconciles monthly: (a) total duties paid vs. BOC assessment; (b) VAT paid at customs vs. input VAT claimed on BIR 2550M; (c) FTA preferential duty savings vs. standard rates; (d) identify classification discrepancies for correction
Responsible (R): Finance – Tax
Accountable (A): Customs Broker
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1233_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1233_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1233_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1233_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-244 (ensure controlled execution — Import &amp; Customs Operations (PA-02.2).)
Owner: Customs Broker / Import Specialist</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
