    <bpmn:process id="W_W1264" name="W1264. Import Container Consolidation, Multi-Vendor FCL Assembly &amp; Space Optimization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — weekly container consolidation cycle; triggered when multiple LCL (less-than-container-load) import POs from the same origin region can be consolidated into FCL (full container load)
Frequency: Weekly consolidation planning; ~400–600 TEUs/month across all import origins
Volume: ~20–30 container bookings per week; ~60% currently FCL, ~40% LCL — target: reduce LCL to 20% through consolidation
Owner: Import Coordinator
Participants: Buyer, Freight Forwarder, Customs Broker, DC Operations Manager, Finance Controller
Source: workflow W1264 — Import Container Consolidation, Multi-Vendor FCL Assembly &amp; Space Optimization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1264_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1264_Lane1" name="Import Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1264_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1264_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1264_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1264_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1264_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1264_Lane2" name="Finance Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1264_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1264_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1264_Start4" name="Scheduled — weekly container consolidation cycle; triggered when multiple LCL…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1264_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1264_Task5" name="Weekly consolidation planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly consolidation planning: Import Coordinator reviews all open import POs: (a) group POs by origin port/region (South China, East China, Taiwan, Southeast Asia, Europe); (b) for each region, calculate total CBM and weight of all open POs; (c) identify consolidation opportunities: (i) if total CBM for a region ≥ 28 CBM (FCL 20ft) or ≥ 58 CBM (FCL 40ft), consolidate into FCL; (ii) if near FCL threshold, check with Buyer for additional POs that could be pulled forward to fill the container; (iii) if below threshold, evaluate holding POs for 1 week to accumulate more volume vs. shipping LCL to meet DC delivery schedule
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 4 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1264_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1264_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1264_Task6" name="Multi-vendor FCL assembly">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Multi-vendor FCL assembly: For consolidated FCL shipments: (a) coordinate with freight forwarder to arrange vendor factory delivery to consolidation warehouse at origin; (b) communicate required delivery date to each vendor — all PO goods must arrive at consolidation warehouse by cut-off date; (c) freight forwarder receives goods from multiple vendors, inspects quantity and packaging, and loads into single container; (d) system generates consolidated packing list with per-vendor breakdown and per-PO breakdown; (e) verify container loading plan: heavy items at bottom, fragile items protected, maximum CBM utilization
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator / Freight Forwarder
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 3 hours per consolidation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1264_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1264_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1264_Task7" name="Rate negotiation &amp; booking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Rate negotiation &amp; booking: Import Coordinator negotiates FCL freight rate and books vessel space: (a) obtain FCL rates from 2–3 freight forwarders for the route; (b) compare FCL consolidated rate vs. sum of individual LCL rates — confirm consolidation savings; (c) book earliest available vessel with transit time meeting DC delivery schedule; (d) confirm container type: standard 20ft/40ft, high-cube (for voluminous but light items like insulation), or open-top (for oversized items); (e) issue booking confirmation to all vendors in the consolidation
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2 hours per booking</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1264_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1264_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1264_Task8" name="Consolidation cost allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Consolidation cost allocation: Finance team allocates consolidated freight cost to individual POs: (a) total freight cost = FCL rate + origin consolidation warehouse fee + documentation fee; (b) allocate to each PO proportionally by: (i) CBM (volumetric allocation), or (ii) weight (weight allocation), whichever produces the charge; (c) add allocated freight cost to each PO&#x27;s landed cost calculation per W2B.12; (d) system updates PO landed cost estimate for accurate margin calculation
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2 hours per consolidation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1264_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1264_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1264_Task9" name="Monthly consolidation performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly consolidation performance review: Import Coordinator reviews monthly consolidation metrics: (a) container utilization rate — average CBM per container vs. capacity; (b) FCL vs. LCL ratio — trend towards higher FCL percentage; (c) freight cost per CBM — compare consolidated vs. non-consolidated; (d) transit time comparison — consolidated FCL vs. LCL; (e) consolidation savings — total PHP saved per month from FCL consolidation vs. LCL alternative; (f) present results to Procurement Manager and Finance Controller
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): Procurement Manager
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1264_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1264_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1264_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1264_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1264_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-244 (ensure controlled execution — Import &amp; Customs Operations (PA-02.2).) | - operational: Import Coordinator review and approval gate
Owner: Import Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
